Let $K$ be a finite field, $G$ a group, and $a,b\in K[G]$ satisfy $ab=1$. Put $M=\operatorname{supp}(b)$ and define $$\label{eq:ca-rule}
  \phi:K^M\longrightarrow K,
  \qquad \phi(p)=\sum_{u\in M}b_up(u).$$ The cellular automaton $\tau=T_b$ is injective, and $$\label{eq:ca-image}
  \operatorname{im}(\tau)=\{y\in K^G:T_{ba}y=y\}.$$ If $ba\ne1$, every $h\in G$ with $(ba-1)_h\ne0$ gives a configuration $\delta_h\notin\operatorname{im}(\tau)$; hence $\tau$ is not surjective.
